    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. i'll try to watch the sleep and protein. but i've also seen people talk about how mental resistance is a thing, like just feeling unmotivated or like some weird psychological wall stops you from finishing a rep even when you aren't physically hurt. do you have any advice for when that happens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a very common experience, often called a \"psychological wall,\" and it usually feels exactly like you've physically hit your limit. To deal with it, focus your attention entirely on your breathing for the final two seconds before the miss, which can help you maintain form and push through. If you can't get both feet off the floor on your next set or maintain perfect technique, consider backing off slightly next time to build confidence. This temporary mental block is actually a sign of good progress, not a reason to quit.",
      "source": "target",
